comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:02:44.778Z",codex-root,Live schema proof found root keys entities/entity_categories and the documented compact field union; only counts and field names are retained.
  "2026-07-24T21:16:54.266Z",codex-root,"Focused transport and command tests pass; full coverage reached 100 percent statements branches functions and lines across 1214 tests; live built CLI passed compact count, raw/decoded structural checks, all six formats, and external settings wizard validation."
  "2026-07-24T21:35:31.713Z",codex-root,"Final exact-tree validation: 1,220 tests and 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; built binary live E2E passed using external settings/auth, including raw and decoded compact display output across TOON, JSON, compact JSON, YAML, table, and Markdown."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:02:44.778Z",codex-root,"Do not expose raw entity rows, device IDs, areas, labels, names, icons, or user details in PM or GitHub evidence."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:02:44.778Z",codex-root,The compact endpoint excludes disabled entities and encodes entity categories by index; decoded output must resolve ec through entity_categories.
  "2026-07-24T21:16:55.618Z",codex-root,A separate decoded view preserves the upstream compact contract and category index map while giving agents stable semantic keys only when requested.
  "2026-07-24T21:49:50.196Z",codex-root,Home Assistant's display registry is an enabled-entity projection optimized for UI bandwidth; preserving raw compact keys by default and offering explicit semantic decoding gives agents a lossless token/cognition tradeoff.
